{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Sba7qb9gWvQsDN2Mox7EkN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Anchor R&D Surface v2 â€” Master Plan (planning trio session) â€” Grounded Summary\n\n**Goal / North Star (locked)**\n- Make Anchor's R&D surface a **truthful, useful memory** of each project's trio work â€” the lane status must reflect *activity*, not masquerade it as empty.\n- **Imported history is first-class history**: a brownfield-discovered trio run counts as real project history, not a second-class `import` placeholder. An honest \"imported\" provenance chip is acceptable, but it is a per-card label, not the lane's whole state.\n- **One trio run = one session**: a research/plan/build run is presented as a single clean session summary the user reads â€” not as N separate per-file cards.\n\n**Key design decisions**\n- **Interactive terminal substrate = stream-json REPL, not ConPTY.** A true ConPTY terminal would require a native dependency, violating Anchor's stdlib-only / no-compiled-assets rule. v2 instead keeps the terminal *feel* over a **persistent `stream-json` REPL**: one long-lived `claude`/`gemini` process per session, user turns POSTed to stdin, assistant output streamed back via **SSE** (replacing the prior 1.5s poll).\n- The REPL **generalizes the existing gate-stdin mechanism**, auto-seeds the correct trio skill per lane, and on process exit **auto-discovers produced files** and asks the user to confirm adoption as a session.\n\n**Follow-up decision (user-driven, 2026-06-11) â€” real xterm.js swap: GO**\n- User chose **real xterm.js** over the lightweight `anchor-term` console.\n- Executed: vendored real `@xterm/xterm 6.0.0` (offline copy, MIT LICENSE + PROVENANCE) into `vendor/xterm/`; rewrote `vendor/anchor-term/anchor-term.js` as an **adapter** over `new window.Terminal(...)` preserving the same `window.AnchorTerm.mount` API, gates, discoverâ†’adopt panel, and `beforeunload` reap.\n- Added a traversal-safe `/vendor/xterm/` static route plus includes (xterm loaded before anchor-term).\n- Backend `rnd_terminal.py` and the SSE/term endpoints were left **byte-unchanged** (verified via an empty git diff).\n- Gate result (orchestrator-run): **394 passed** (the anchor text is truncated mid-line, so the full gate tally is not fully stated in the source).\n\n**Member documents this session draws on**\n- Anchor R&D Surface v2 â€” Master Plan (frozen design)\n- Anchor R&D Surface v2 â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n- Anchor R&D Surface v2 â€” Execution Log\n\n---\n*Note: the xterm gate line in the source anchors is truncated (\"â€¦1 s\"), so the complete pass/skip count for that follow-up is not fully recoverable from the provided material.*"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a2a472b-11f7-4682-a408-587be823782a","uuid":"8d8644bf-1c09-401c-96d1-81bd6a7c301a","request_id":"req_011Cc1hYEteo1jTt2ZgVz4CP"}
